course: dictionary
lesson: 5079
title: Insulators
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: An insulator is a material that slows down the movement of heat or electricity through it. Wool, plastic foam and air trapped in tiny pockets are good at keeping heat in, so a woolly hat keeps your head warm.
explain: Plastic, rubber, wood and glass are good at stopping electricity. That is why plastic covers on wires and plugs keep electricity away from your hands.
explain: Some materials, such as plastic and wood, can be insulators for both heat and electricity. Insulators can keep heat in, like a flask, or keep heat out, like a cool box.
explain: The opposite of an insulator is a conductor. Metals are good conductors, so they let heat and electricity pass through them easily.
fact: An insulator is a material that does not let heat or electricity pass through it easily.
fact: «Air trapped in wool, feathers or double windows is a good insulator.»
fact: «Insulators also keep cold things cold, like food in a cool box.»
fact: Plastic, rubber, wood and glass are electrical insulators, which is why wires are metal inside and covered in plastic.
fact: A conductor, such as metal, is the opposite of an insulator because it lets heat or electricity move through it easily.
exercise: «Air trapped in wool, feathers or double windows is a good insulator.» What is a good insulator? | A torch | *A material that does not let heat pass through easily | A material that lets heat pass through easily | A metal spoon
exercise: Why are wires metal inside and covered in plastic? | So the wire glows in the dark | To make the wire heavier | So the wire can be bent more easily | *So electricity stays in the wire and cannot reach our hands
exercise: Which of these is a conductor, not an insulator? | Plastic | *Iron | Wool | Cork
test: Which material is a good thermal insulator? | Steel | *Wool | Iron | Glass
test: «Insulators also keep cold things cold, like food in a cool box.» What does a cool box do? | Makes electricity flow through the food | *Keeps cold things cold by slowing heat getting in | Turns water into ice | Makes food hot
exam: Ella wraps her hot drink in a woolly sleeve. Why is wool a useful insulator? | Because it conducts heat quickly | Because it is made of metal | *Because it slows down heat moving through it | Because it lets electricity flow through it
